  "spec_review": {
    "verdict": "pass",
    "reasons": [
      "The model-specific inventory is a typed host-only core module. The host uses it after completed preparation; generic input/work/config/Skill inventory, native publisher and workflow remain byte-identical to C2.",
      "The bounded Linux model store walk holds directory descriptors, uses no-follow opens, rejects directory links and special files, verifies before/after identities and all content-addressed blob bytes, and does not follow raw named links through the kernel.",
      "Canonical named v2 lookup has priority over legacy lookup. Named manifest identity is bound to exact bytes and either a direct API digest or a bounded manifest-list parent, unique selected child, selected leaf bytes, API digest and runner.",
      "Raw model symlink targets must equal the official canonical relative expression. The earlier lexical cancellation flaw is closed without broadening general symlink or artifact publication policy.",
      "Existing strict_json parsing enforces explicit 1 MiB and 32-level limits, duplicate-key and non-finite rejection. Unsupported nested/inline/ambiguous model lists fail closed.",
      "The result and receipt notes distinguish successful hosted model preparation from failed full inventory freeze and zero task runs. They do not convert synthetic tests into native acceptance, Skill loading, usage, session or efficacy evidence."
    ]
  },
  "quality_review": {
    "verdict": "pass",
    "reasons": [
      "Read all frozen implementation and new regression tests, host integration diff, requirements/design/tasks, and archived outcome facts; no remaining concrete blocker found.",
      "Independently reproduced the pre-fix raw-link flaw using a synthetic filesystem. Actual ELOOP differed from the draft's acceptance; the original negative receipt is retained unchanged.",
      "Author evidence shows 36 test methods (19 new, 17 existing) and 52 actual subTest callbacks passing in 1.426 seconds, with mypy on five files, Ruff, formatting, module-size and security checks passing.",
      "The separate repository full regression completed 102 of 102 registered gates with exit 0, empty stderr and no frozen-source drift. The raw timing, command result and streams agree.",
      "The 23-member author wrapper and 4-member full wrapper reconstruct exact UTF-8 source bytes. All declared lengths and SHA256 values match original scratch evidence; no mismatches were found.",
      "Seven final staged receipts match scratch originals and Git index bytes. Fifteen frozen file identities still match source E, index and working tree; no unstaged changes were observed.",
      "Post-full security and staged-diff receipts report a clean check over 2105 Git inventory files, without changing the scanner or source."
    ]
  },
  "verdict": "pass",
  "open_findings": [],
  "closed_findings": [
